`check-layers` on a three-crate table (check-layers.in/): the workspace that
follows it passes; the one where `core` depends on `lsp` fails.

```console
$ xtask check-layers --layers layers.toml --metadata downward.json
check-layers: 3 crates in 2 layers; all 3 dependencies between them point down

$ xtask check-layers --layers layers.toml --metadata upward.json
? 1
error: `core` (foundation tier 0) has a normal dependency on `lsp` (application tier 0), a higher place: a crate may depend only on crates of a lower layer, or of a lower tier of its own layer
check-layers: 1 violation(s) of the layer table (layers.toml)

$ xtask check-layers --layers layers.toml --metadata
? 2
xtask check-layers: --metadata needs a FILE

$ xtask check-layers --layers missing.toml
? 2
xtask check-layers: read missing.toml: [..]

```
